  "details": "When calling GetComponent(Type) on a GameObject without the component and the type is a built in Unity component, the program will crash. The security blacklist check believes the object is not actually null, while the UnityObject is null. Note this does not happen when using GetComponent<T>\n[<color=yellow>UdonBehaviour</color>] An exception occurred during Udon execution, this UdonBehaviour will be halted.\nVRC.Udon.VM.UdonVMException: The VM encountered an error!\nException Message:\n  An exception occurred during EXTERN to 'UnityEngineGameObject.__GetComponent__SystemType__UnityEngineComponent'.\n      Parameter Addresses: 0x00000000, 0x00000001, 0x00000003\n  \n  There is no 'Rigidbody' attached to the \"GameObject\" game object, but a script is trying to access it.\nYou probably need to add a Rigidbody to the game object \"GameObject\". Or your script needs to check if the component is attached before using it.\nGraph asset:\napplication/vnd.unity.graphview.elements ",
